    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d95-a1">

                <pb facs="0099" n="87" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg87"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Annex—Extracts]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Acting Chief of the Division of
                        European Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-10-30">October 30, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>4. <hi rendition="#italic">Finland</hi>. The Finns are now divided in their
                    political opinions but a British declaration of war would unify the nation
                    versus the British and would force the nation into German arms which is not now
                    the case. This would immediately intensify Finland’s war efforts and increase
                    the peril of supplies to Russia and the Archangel route. This would likewise
                    intensify Finland’s effort against Leningrad.</p>
                <p>Such a declaration of war would undoubtedly have repercussions in Sweden
                    unfavorable to the democracies.</p>
                <pb facs="0100" n="88" xml:id="pg88"/>
                <p>Our restraining influence in Finland would be destroyed.</p>
                <p>If the Soviets desire by this declaration of war that British troops should
                    attack Finland, Great Britain might well announce her effort as an attack on
                    those <hi rendition="#italic">German</hi> forces occupying Petsamo and Northern
                    Finland without any declaration of war.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>A declaration of war would not at this time facilitate British military effort,
                    it would merely be a gesture to placate Russia and could be used by Germany as a
                    favorable argument in mobilizing all of Eastern Europe against the democracies
                    and the implied threat to the future of the small countries of Eastern Europe
                    through Soviet ambitions at the peace table.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>R[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ay</hi>] A[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >therton</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
